"text": "Getting started 1. Install # Tested on Windows with Python 3.11.9, PyTorch 2.5.1 (CUDA 12.1) and an NVIDIA RTX 4060 Laptop GPU. pip install -r requirements.txt Install the PyTorch build that matches your CUDA version from pytorch.org . 2. Get the data # The datasets are not included in the repository. Download them and place them as shown. Dataset Download Put it in It should contain CBIS-DDSM (JPEG version) Kaggle · original DICOM release on TCIA data/CBIS-DDSM/ csv/ and jpeg/ INbreast On request from the dataset authors ( paper ) data/INbreast/ AllDICOMs/ and INbreast.csv (or .xls ) If your data is stored somewhere else, point to it with environment variables instead: Windows (PowerShell) Linux / macOS $env:CBIS_DDSM_DIR = \"D:\\datasets\\CBIS-DDSM\" $env:INBREAST_DIR = \"D:\\datasets\\INbreast\" export CBIS_DDSM_DIR = /data/CBIS-DDSM export INBREAST_DIR = /data/INbreast 3. Run the experiments # Run everything from the repository folder, starting with the main experiment. Later scripts reuse its results and its image cache. # Training python experiments/main_cbis_ddsm.py python experiments/method_comparison.py python experiments/calibration_experiment.py python experiments/inbreast_validation.py --data-root data/INbreast python experiments/shortcut_strength_sweep.py --seeds 5 python experiments/backbone_density_variants.py --seeds 5 python experiments/weight_and_grl_sweeps.py --study distcorr python experiments/weight_and_grl_sweeps.py --study camreg python experiments/weight_and_grl_sweeps.py --study grl python experiments/full_weight_grid.py # Analysis (no training) python analysis/density_split_report.py python analysis/mask_audit.py --full-res python analysis/calibration_analysis.py calibration --dir outputs/calibration_experiment python analysis/density_probe_metrics.py --dir outputs/calibration_experiment python analysis/tables_and_figures.py python analysis/paper_figures.py Handy options # Script Option What it does main_cbis_ddsm.py , method_comparison.py --seeds N Use only the first N seeds Other experiment scripts --dry-run Show the planned runs and data sizes without training Other experiment scripts --smoke A quick one-seed run to test the setup Other experiment scripts --help List every option Working on this website # The website is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript in the docs/ folder, with no build step. Preview it: run python -m http.server -d docs 8000 and open http://127.0.0.1:8000, or open docs/index.html directly. Edit a page: each page is one HTML file, for example docs/results/main.html . Styles are in docs/assets/css/site.css and behaviour in docs/assets/js/site.js . Publish it: on GitHub, open Settings → Pages , choose Deploy from a branch , and select the main branch and the /docs folder. Adding the figures # The figure slots on this site show a placeholder until the image file exists. Save your figures in docs/assets/figures/ with these names: File name Where it comes from Shown on architecture.png Your pipeline diagram (rename architecture 2.png ) Home, Method dccam_qualitative_gradcam.png outputs/main_experiment/ Main comparison forest_plot_main.png outputs/paper_figures/ Main comparison shortcut_and_weight_sweeps.png outputs/paper_figures/ Loss weights and shortcut strength grl_configurations.png outputs/paper_figures/ Adversaries and published methods"
