"text": "Glossary Short forms # Term Meaning ACR American College of Radiology (density grades used in INbreast) AUROC Area under the ROC curve: how well a model ranks cancers above benign cases (0.5 = chance, 1 = perfect) BI-RADS The standard system radiologists use for reporting; its density grades run from A to D CAM Class activation map: a heat map of which image areas drove the prediction CBIS-DDSM A curated public collection of scanned film mammograms CI Confidence interval CLUB A method that reduces mutual information between features and an attribute DistCorr / dCor Distance correlation: a measure of any kind of dependence between two variables ECE Expected calibration error: how far predicted probabilities are from real frequencies FDR False discovery rate GAP Global average pooling Grad-CAM A common way of drawing a CAM heat map from a trained network GRL Gradient reversal layer: the core of adversarial removal Group DRO A training method that focuses on the worst-off group JTT Just Train Twice: retrains with extra weight on the examples a first model got wrong MI Mutual information MINE A neural estimator of mutual information, used here as a penalty SAS Spurious attribution score: the share of the heat map outside the breast SD Standard deviation TCIA The Cancer Imaging Archive, which hosts CBIS-DDSM Key ideas # Shortcut An easy cue that happens to go along with the label in the training data, which the model uses instead of the real signal. Aligned group Test cases that fit the shortcut: a dense cancer, or a non-dense benign case. Conflicting group Test cases that break the shortcut: a non-dense cancer, or a dense benign case. A shortcut-reliant model struggles here. Group gap AUROC on the aligned group minus AUROC on the conflicting group. The main measure in this work; smaller is fairer. Density probe A simple classifier trained on the model's features to guess density. If it guesses well, density is still in the features. Adding the shortcut Sampling the training data so that density and cancer go together (r ≈ 0.6), while the validation and test data stay untouched. Symbols # Symbol Meaning \\(\\alpha\\) Significance level of a test (here 0.05) \\(\\mathrm{AUROC}_a\\) AUROC on the aligned group \\(\\mathrm{AUROC}_c\\) AUROC on the conflicting group \\(\\mathrm{CAM}_i\\) Heat-map value at pixel \\(i\\) (normalized, never negative) \\(\\Delta_{\\text{gap}}\\) Group gap, \\(\\mathrm{AUROC}_a - \\mathrm{AUROC}_c\\) \\(J\\) Youden's J: sensitivity + specificity − 1 \\(\\lambda\\) Reversal strength, or the weight of a penalty \\(\\lambda_{\\max}\\) Highest reversal strength \\(M_i\\) Breast mask at pixel \\(i\\) : 1 inside, 0 outside \\(n\\) Number of paired runs \\(p\\) Wilcoxon signed-rank p-value \\(r\\) Correlation between density and cancer \\(w\\) Weight of the adversarial loss"
